.\"
.Dd
.Dt ARCHIVEMOUNT 1
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm archivemount
.Nd mount an archive for access as a file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hVdfs
.Op Fl o Ar option Ns Oo , Ns Ar option Oc Ns …
.Ar archive
.Ar mountpoint
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Mounts file tree contained in
.Ar archive
on directory
.Ar mountpoint .
.Xr umount 8
can later reverse this mapping.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -compact
.Li $ Nm ls
files.tar.gz    mnt/
.Li $ Nm tar Fl tf Pa files.tar.gz
file1
file2
.Li $ Nm Pa files.tar.gz mnt
.Li $ Nm ls mnt
file1           file2
.Li $ Ic echo Li zupa > Pa mnt/file3
.Li $ Nm rm Pa mnt/file1
.Li $ Nm umount Pa mnt
.Li $ Nm ls
files.tar.gz    files.tar.gz.orig               mnt/
.Li $ Nm tar Fl tf Pa files.tar.gz
file2
file3
.Ed
.
.Sh OPTIONS
See
.Xr fuse 8
for a complete list of the baseline FUSE options supported.
The following options are handled specially by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -compact -width ".Fl o Cm subtree Ns = Ns Ar regex"
.It Fl h , -help
Write usage and all available options to standard error stream, then exit
.Sy 1 .
.
.It Fl V , -version
Write version of
.Nm
and its dependencies to standard output and error streams (intermingled), then exit.
.Pp
.
.It Fl o Cm readonly , Fl o Cm ro , Fl r
Disable writes entirely.
.
.It Fl o Cm password
Prompt for archive passphrase.
.
.It Fl o Cm nobackup
When saving writes, the original
.Ar archive
is moved to
.Qq Ar archive Ns Li .orig .
This flag removes that file afterward.
.
.It Fl o Cm nosave
Allow writes, but don't write them out.
.Pp
.
.It Fl o Cm subtree Ns = Ns Ar regex
Hide files not matching
.Ar regex ,
and on those that do match, remove the match from the filename.
.Ar regex
is a basic regular expression that behaves as-if prepended with the equivalent of
.Qq Li ^.? .
Implies
.Fl o Cm readonly .
.
.It Fl o Cm formatraw
.Ar archive
is actually a file, exposed verbatim
.Em but uncompressed
as
.Ar mounpoint Ns Pa /data .
Implies
.Fl o Cm readonly .
.El
.
.Sh BUGS
Writing archives, probably.
.
.Sh ARCHIVE FORMATS
See
.Xr libarchive 3
for a definitive list, but
all kinds of tar/ustar/pax/cpio archives, 7-Zip, ISO9660 CDs, ar, and RAR/Zip may be read.
These may be compressed with
.Xr gzip 1 ,
.Xr xz 1 ,
.Xr zstd 1 ,
&c. and are processed transparently.
The same applies for writing (except you can't write RARs).
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libarchive 3 ,
.Xr regex 7 ,
.Xr fuse 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
